<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Westminster, Vermont</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Westminster is a town in south-eastern Vermont, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/connecticut-river">Connecticut River</a>. A convention held there in January 1777 declared the independence of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-hampshire-grants">New Hampshire Grants</a> as the state of New <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/connecticut">Connecticut</a>, soon renamed Vermont. It was also the scene of the Westminster Massacre of March 1775.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/westminster-vermont.jpg" alt="Westminster, Vermont" width="320" height="248" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Putneypics · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Westminster_Town_Hall.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
